170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 72 0 R
/E (This imbalance jeopardizes trust, which is essential for markets and democracies. In leadership discourse, "soulless AI" arises when businesses prioritize speed and size, when leaders evade accountability, and when education generates proficient operators without fostering discerning citizens. The paramount threat is not an aware machine, but an unconscious humanity potent yet underdeveloped.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 72 0 R
/E (If "soulless AI" represents intelligence devoid of moral guidance, then "AI with soul" signifies AI integrated inside a human, ethical, & cultural context. The aim is not to idealize technology but to refine it. AI with a soul can be delineated by seven criteria. concepts that convert ethical aspirations into institutional implementation.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 72 0 R
/E (1\) Human dignity is the necessary foundation. Systems must be engineered to safeguard the inherent value of each individual. This encompasses honoring privacy, preventing humiliation, and guaranteeing that individuals are not diminished to mere data entities.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
173 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 72 0 R
/E (2\) Beneficence and non-maleficence. Artificial intelligence should strive to promote beneficial outcomes and mitigate harm, informed by evaluations of real-world effects. This encompasses forecasting secondary effects and unforeseen repercussions.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 72 0 R
/E (3\) Equity and inclusivity. Fairness must be deliberately constructed through data governance, bias assessment, and inclusive design. Inclusion entails accessibility & reverence for cultural variety.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 72 0 R
/E (4\) Clarity and elucidation. When judgments impact rights or life possibilities, and individuals must comprehend the rationale, possess viable avenues for redress. Transparency encompasses the disclosure of AI utilization.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 72 0 R
/E (5\) Responsibility. Responsibility must be allocated and enforceable within organizations and throughout supplier chains. The Ethical governance necessitates designated proprietors and recorded decision-making processes.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 72 0 R
/E (6\) Proportionality. Not every issue necessitates artificial intelligence. The appropriate degree of automation must be determined based on risk assessment and human values. Occasionally, more straightforward regulations are safer and more legitimate.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 72 0 R
/E (7\) Education for autonomy. Users ought to be enabled to engage in critical thinking rather than simply absorb infor- mation. Artificial intelligence should serve as an instrument for education and decision making assistance, rather than a replacement for moral judgment.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
