186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (In a culture that venerates disruption, and constraints may be perceived as frailty. However, boundaries signify the essence of adulthood. An established institution may assert: we will refrain from using a system if we cannot elucidate its functioning; we will not pursue automation. A choice impacting rights without human oversight; we will refrain from data collection absent transparency; we will not excuse ourselves with "the algorithm dictated my actions." Const-   -raints must be integrated into procurement, compliance, and leadership assessment. Ethical leadership in artificial intelligence is fundamentally a relational discipline. Trust is established when stakeholders are acknowledged, when damages are rectified, and when openness transcends mere marketing rhetoric to become an operational principle. This illustrates the inadequacy of ethics committees alone: the overarching culture It is imperative to incentivize approp-    -riate conduct and penalize negligence. Ultimately, the soul as a guiding principle reestablishes the connection between technology and service. It inquires: In what manner does this system mitigate suffering? In what manner does it enhance inclusion? In what ways does it enhance significance and foster community? When such inquiries become commonplace, AI transforms into an instrument for human flourishing rather than a extraction force. In the context of leadership, power transforms into service rather than oppression.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
