/E (Institutions can integrate three sources of the evidence to implement these indicators. Initially, quantitative assess-     -ment \(audit outcomes, complaint frequencies, escalation rates, demographic effects\). Secondly, qualitative listening encompasses focus groups, interviews, citizen panels, and employee dialogues. Third case based ethical analysis  where in challenging occurrences are examined comprehensively, encompassing the emotional and societal ramifications. This triangulation averts "dashboard ethics," wherein numerical data obscures the truth.Defining thresholds and reaction protocols is also essential. For instance, if the inclusion score falls below a specified threshold, the system must be suspended and re-evaluated; if indicators of psychological safety diminish, leadership must ascertain whether AI is )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [17]
>>
