/E (Case 2: Artificial Intelligence in Education. A university use artificial intelligence to produce feedback for essays. If misused, pupils may delegate their learning and develop dependency. AI with soul reconfigures testing to require students to articulate reasoning, reference sources, and the contemplate their learning. Artificial Intelligence evolves into a Instructor for cognitive development, not a replace-    -ment for diligence. The institution establishes an integrity policy: AI may provide assistance, although authorship and accountability reside with the student.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (Case 4: Artificial Intelligence in hospital triage. A model forecasts danger and prioritizes treatment. Opaque models can cause harm to patients. AI possessing a soul necessitates transparency, clinical responsibility informed consent where feasible, and governance that regards blunders as significant occurrences. Clinicians must recognize that the model is consultative, not prescriptive.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (Case 3: Artificial Intelligence in Customer Service. A public institution use chatbots to manage citizen inquiries. An insensitive bot might demean vulnerable individuals. AI with consciousness necessitates respectful language, empat-  -hetic protocols, escalation pathways & ongoing surveillance of citizens. experience. Accessibility is also essential: the system must be operable by elderly individuals and those with disabilities.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 77 0 R
/E (Case 5: AI in Organizational Surveillance. A corporation utilizes AI to enhance efficiency through the analysis of emails, keystrokes, and the meetings. This may enhance efficiency but undermines trust and the dignity. AI with integrity establishes stringent boundaries: privacy by design minimum data acquisition. and an emphasis on promoting  wellbeing rather than the monitoring. These instances exemplify a fundamental principle: ethics is not merely a theoretical discussion; it is a decision in design and a decision in leadership. The paramount decision is not which algorithm to acquire, but rather which culture to cultivate.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
