331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (The primary ethical standard in technology is the limitation. Every inquiry on our capabilities must be complemented by a more profound question: ought we to proceed? The dual  )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (At that juncture, technology acquires a semblance of soul, provided the society employing it has not forfeited its own The key inquiry of our era is not if artificial intelligence will possess a soul, but rather if we will bestow one onto it. Artificial intelligence serves as a reflection of our identity, values, and priorities. The essence of AI is not found within the machine itself, but in the intentions behind its design, the cultural context surrounding it, and the choices we make in private: the data we select, the biases we accept, and the damages we rationalize for the sake of efficiency or expediency. To ensure AI benefits the common good, we want institutions with integrity: colleges that foster discernment rather than merely technical skills; corpora-     -tions that prioritize compassion over optimization; and public frameworks that safeguard dignity above short-term profit. The fundamental inquiry is not what AI will impose upon us, but rather how we will utilize the myriad possibilities that AI presents. This pertains to a matter of leadership. Ultimately, it pertains to the essence of the soul. The future requires more than mere intelligence. It requires heightened awareness, enhanced ethics, and increased humanity. The genuine advancement of our society is in the equilibrium between technology and the human spirit.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
